{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"For a US open-end ETF, the board may designate the fund’s **investment adviser** as valuation designee—provided it is not a sub-adviser primarily responsible for portfolio management of the fund (or another fund in the same group). The board cannot delegate valuation responsibility to a third-party pricing service.\n\nThe adviser must report to the board **at least quarterly** on matters materially affecting fair-value determinations, including significant valuation process deficiencies or material weaknesses, and any material changes in valuation risks or methodologies. It must also report **promptly** any matter materially affecting the fair value of a portfolio investment, including significant events warranting board attention."}}
